<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/roman-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Roman%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Roman Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gothic forces kill Emperor Valens and much of the Eastern field army at Adrianople</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/teotihuacan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Teotihuacan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Teotihuacan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Siyaj K’ak’ arrives at Tikal, and a new king linked to Teotihuacan takes power</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/alemanni"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Alemanni.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Alemanni</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gratian’s army defeats the Lentienses at Argentaria in Alsace</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tikal"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tikal.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tikal</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sihyaj K'ahk', linked with Teotihuacan, arrives and King Chak Tok Ich'aak I dies</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/maya-civilisation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Maya%20civilisation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Maya civilisation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Siyaj K’ak', a war leader linked with Teotihuacan, arrives at Tikal and a new dynasty takes power</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/el-peru-waka"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/El%20Per%C3%BA-Waka'.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>El Perú-Waka'</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Teotihuacan war leader Siyaj K'ahk' arrives at Waka' in January, ten days before reaching Tikal: La Entrada, the first recorded meeting of Teotihuacan and the Maya.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-adrianople"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Adrianople.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Adrianople</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Valens reaches Constantinople on 30 May and sends Sebastianus to reorganise the armies in Thrace</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-adrianople"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Adrianople.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Adrianople</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 8 August Fritigern offers peace and an alliance in exchange for Roman territory, and Valens refuses</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-adrianople"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Adrianople.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Adrianople</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 9 August the Romans march out from Adrianople and are routed by the Goths and their cavalry, and Valens dies</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-adrianople"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Adrianople.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Adrianople</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Goths try and fail to take Adrianople</span></li></ul></section>
